nd its principles, by a Tokyo-based teacher.","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/198425/washoku-by-elizabeth-andoh/","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781580085199"},{"name":"Japanese Cooking: A Simple Art","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Shizuo Tsuji, 1980","note":"Classic technique-focused reference from the founder of an Osaka cooking school; ISBN is the Kodansha anniversary edition.","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/563613/japanese-cooking-by-shizuo-tsuji-introduction-by-mfk-fisher-foreword-by-ruth-reichl-preface-byyoshiki-tsuji/","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781568363882"},{"name":"Japan: The Cookbook","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Nancy Singleton Hachisu, 2018","note":"Large Phaidon compendium of Japanese home recipes by a writer who has lived on a farm in Japan for decades.","url":"https://www.phaidon.com/en-us/products/japan-the-cookbook","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Nori","ingredient/nori"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Dashi","ingredient/dashi"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Aspergillus oryzae","ingredient/aspergillus-oryzae"],["Soybean","ingredient/soybean"],["Mirin","ingredient/mirin"],["Katsuobushi","ingredient/katsuobushi"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Surimi","ingredient/surimi"],["Bread crumbs","ingredient/bread-crumbs"],["Japanese curry","ingredient/japanese-curry"],["Unagi","ingredient/unagi"],["Offal","ingredient/offal"],["Grasshopper","ingredient/grasshopper"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Cream cheese","ingredient/cream-cheese"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Within Japanese cooking","count":9,"links":[["Ainu cuisine","cuisine/ainu-cuisine"],["Hawaiian cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-hawaii"],["Itameshi","cuisine/itameshi"],["Japanese Chinese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine"],["Japanese regional cuisine","cuisine/japanese-regional-cuisine"],["Japanese-American cuisine","cuisine/japanese-american-cuisine"],["Kaiseki","cuisine/kaiseki"],["Okinawan cuisine","cuisine/okinawan-cuisine"],["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku"]]},{"h":"More from Japan","count":2,"links":[["Nagoya cuisine","cuisine/nagoya-cuisine"],["Shippoku","cuisine/shippoku"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/f/f7/Breakfast_at_Tamahan_Ryokan%2C_Kyoto.jpg/500px-Breakfast_at_Tamahan_Ryokan%2C_Kyoto.jpg","w":500,"h":294,"by":"MichaelMaggs","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Breakfast_at_Tamahan_Ryokan%2C_Kyoto.jpg"}},"cuisine/anhui-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/anhui-cuisine","n":"Anhui cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[["Anhui cuisine, alternatively referred to as Hui cuisine, is one of the Eight Culinary Traditions of Chinese cuisine. It is derived from the native cooking styles of the Huangshan region in southern Anhui Province."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"anhui-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anhui_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"ingredient/banana":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/banana","n":"Banana","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 12 dishes across 10 cuisines","intro":[["A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa. In some countries, cooking bananas are called plantains, distinguishing them from dessert bananas. The fruit is variable in size, color and firmness, but is usually elongated and curved, with soft flesh rich in starch covered with a peel, which may have a variety of colors when ripe. It grows upward in clusters near the top of the plant. Almost all modern edible seedless (parthenocarp) cultivated bananas come from two wild species – Musa acuminata and Musa balbisiana, or their hybrids."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-banana"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":10,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Kolak (food)","dish/kolak-food"],["Kue bugis","dish/kue-bugis"],["Kue leker","dish/kue-leker"],["Rujak soto","dish/rujak-soto"],["Timphan","dish/timphan"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"]]],["Acehnese cuisine","cuisine/acehnese-cuisine",[["Timphan","dish/timphan"]]],["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Banana ketchup","dish/banana-ketchup"]]],["Gujarati cuisine","cuisine/gujarati-cuisine",[["Undhiyu","dish/undhiyu"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Banana ketchup","dish/banana-ketchup"]]],["Moroccan cuisine","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",[["Zaazaa","dish/zaazaa"]]],["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine",[["Flying Jacob","dish/flying-jacob"]]],["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine",[["Riz Casimir","dish/riz-casimir"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Banana ketchup","dish/banana-ketchup"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Bananas","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":133940574,"top":[["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",34883072],["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",11695300],["Indonesia","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",8952990],["Brazil","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",6853478],["Ecuador","cuisine/ecuadorian-cuisine",6729539],["Nigeria","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine",6695328],["Philippines","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",5861954],["Angola","cuisine/angolan-cuisine",4649246],["Guatemala","cuisine/guatemalan-cuisine",3814668],["Tanzania","cuisine/tanzanian-cuisine",3238383],["Costa Rica","cuisine/costa-rican-cuisine",2609539],["Mexico","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",2555143],["Colombia","cuisine/colombian-cuisine",2505492],["Vietnam","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",2477756],["Peru","cuisine/peruvian-cuisine",2369119]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Pandan","ingredient/pandan"],["Sweet potato","ingredient/sweet-potato"],["Rice flour","ingredient/rice-flour"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Wheat","ingredient/wheat"],["Custard","ingredient/custard"],["Ladyfinger (cookie)","ingredient/ladyfinger-cookie"],["Vanilla Wafers","ingredient/vanilla-wafers"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/d/de/Bananavarieties.jpg","w":500,"h":286,"by":"TimothyPilgrim","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bananavarieties.jpg"}},"dish/chicken-tabaka":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/chicken-tabaka","n":"Chicken tabaka","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Chicken tabaka or chicken tapaka (Georgian: წიწილა ტაფაკა, romanized: ts'its'ila t'apak'a) is a traditional Georgian dish of a pan-fried chicken which is also popular in other Caucasian cuisines. It also became a common restaurant dish in the Soviet cuisine and is found nowadays in many restaurants throughout Eastern Europe and Central Asia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-chicken-tabaka"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken_tabaka"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine"],["Soviet cuisine","cuisine/soviet-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Smetana","ingredient/smetana"],["Tkemali","ingredient/tkemali"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Georgian Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"georgianrecipes.net","note":"Recipe site dedicated to traditional Georgian dishes.","url":"https://georgianrecipes.net/about-georgian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Georgian cuisine","links":[["Achma","dish/achma"],["Ajika","dish/ajika"],["Akhasheni","dish/akhasheni"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chakapuli","dish/chakapuli"],["Chakhokhbili","dish/chakhokhbili"],["Chashushuli","dish/chashushuli"],["Churchkhela","dish/churchkhela"],["Dambalkhacho","dish/dambalkhacho"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["Gozinaki","dish/gozinaki"],["Khachapuri","dish/khachapuri"],["Kharcho","dish/kharcho"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Khvanchkara","dish/khvanchkara"],["Kindzmarauli","dish/kindzmarauli"],["Kubdari","dish/kubdari"],["Kuchmachi","dish/kuchmachi"],["Kvass","dish/kvass"],["Lobiani","dish/lobiani"],["Mchadi","dish/mchadi"],["Mujuretuli","dish/mujuretuli"],["Nadugi","dish/nadugi"],["Nigvziani badrijani","dish/nigvziani-badrijani"],["Pkhali","dish/pkhali"],["Shkmeruli","dish/shkmeruli"],["Tsolikouri","dish/tsolikouri"],["Tvishi (wine)","dish/tvishi-wine"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/4/42/%D0%A6%D1%8B%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BA_%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg/500px-%D0%A6%D1%8B%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BA_%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg","w":500,"h":331,"by":"Pannet","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A6%D1%8B%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BA_%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg"}},"dish/gaifan":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/gaifan","n":"Gaifan","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Gaifan or gaijiaofan (蓋澆飯; 盖浇饭; 'topping on rice') is a type of dish in Chinese cuisine typically offered in low-cost establishments. It consists of a fish, meat, or vegetable topping served over rice. The dish can be either freshly cooked or previously cooked, such as char siu. According to the Commentary to the Classic of Rites, gaifan can be dated back to Western Zhou.  Throughout the Tang dynasty, gaifan was served during the banquets of newly promoted officials."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-gaifan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaifan"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Red House Spice","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chin